  "created_at": "2026-09-04T05:25:33.938Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-09-04T05:27:20.840Z",
  "scope": [
    "Define how a newly initialized project maps Provider-neutral execution profiles to its own available models without chat memory, and freeze separate no-generation successor designs for single-repository maturation and multi-repository cache isolation."
  ],
  "acceptance_criteria": [
    "The framework overlay remains Provider-neutral and does not copy Temple repository model names into adopter projects.",
    "The design separates Provider discovery, compatibility evidence, project policy mapping, route resolution, execution authority, usage observation, calibration, and reviewed policy adoption.",
    "Unknown or unavailable Provider capabilities fail closed; Provider catalog presence is not treated as model quality or cost evidence.",
    "A cold-start project can make a bounded initial mapping and later refine it from matched project-local evidence without automatic self-modification.",
    "Single-repository and multi-repository successor protocols use separate hypotheses, cache controls, sample-size rules, and stop boundaries derived from WI-0143.",
    "This Work Item performs no Provider generation, automatic model execution, external write, or public efficiency claim."
  ],
